# **High-Performance Engineering Report: Native Canvas Interfaces, WebSocket Synchronization, and Procedural Rendering in Phaser 3 Desktop Architectures**

## **Native Canvas UI Architecture and Pixel-Perfect Text Rendering**

Integrating high-performance control panels into graphic rendering environments requires strict adherence to single-context rendering pipelines.1 Forcing the graphics processing unit (GPU) to switch rendering contexts between WebGL canvas draw calls and the browser's document object model (DOM) compositing layers introduces substantial frame time spikes, layout reflow penalties, and input latency.1 To eliminate this overhead, the Ravenstack Fortress visual dashboard implements a pure in-canvas user interface (UI) architecture where all HUD elements, inspection modules, and terminal logs are rendered natively within the WebGL/Canvas context of Phaser 3\.1  
A primary challenge in native canvas UI design is managing container hierarchies and geometry clipping.1 The custom scrollable console engineered for this system extends Phaser.GameObjects.Container.4 Under WebGL rendering pipelines, child masking must be handled carefully due to historical stencil buffer limitations and nested container transformations.4 By applying a parent-level Phaser.Display.Masks.GeometryMask linked to a non-rendered graphic shape, child elements are bounded perfectly without leaking over coordinate thresholds.1  
To maintain crispness on High-DPI (Retina) displays, standard game configurations must disable bilinear filtering and scale the rendering resolution dynamically to prevent sub-pixel interpolation blur.8 Setting the texture-filtering properties and pixel rounding algorithms correctly ensures that low-fidelity pixel fonts and vector geometry preserve sharp edges.8

### **Native Text Render Configuration and Blur Mitigation**

| Configuration Property | Target Value / Type | Architectural Purpose |
| :---- | :---- | :---- |
| gameConfig.pixelArt | true | Disables bilinear interpolation across WebGL textures.8 |
| gameConfig.roundPixels | true | Coordinates rounding calculations directly on the GPU shader to prevent sub-pixel rendering offsets.8 |
| textObject.resolution | window.devicePixelRatio | Multiplies the backing canvas size of the native text object to match the display's physical pixel grid.9 |
| textObject.setScale | 0.5 | Offsets high-resolution texture maps down to fractional scales to produce vector-like edge paths.9 |

### **Complete Scrollable Text Log Console Class**

The following TypeScript module delivers an implementation of a native, scrollable log console utilizing parent-bounded masking, coordinate-locked dragging, and mouse-wheel delta tracking.1

TypeScript  
import \* as Phaser from 'phaser';

export class ScrollableConsole extends Phaser.GameObjects.Container {  
    private textLines: string \=;  
    private textObjects: Phaser.GameObjects.Text \=;  
    private contentContainer: Phaser.GameObjects.Container;  
    private scrollbarTrack: Phaser.GameObjects.Graphics;  
    private scrollbarHandle: Phaser.GameObjects.Graphics;  
    private maskShape: Phaser.GameObjects.Graphics;  

    private consoleWidth: number;  
    private consoleHeight: number;  
    private maxCapacity: number \= 100;  
    private padding: number \= 8;  
    private scrollPercentage: number \= 0;  
    private isDragging: boolean \= false;

    constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene, x: number, y: number, width: number, height: number) {  
        super(scene, x, y);

        this.consoleWidth \= width;  
        this.consoleHeight \= height;

        // Content container holds all dynamically rendered text objects   
        this.contentContainer \= scene.add.container(0, 0);  
        this.add(this.contentContainer);

        // Generate the geometry mask shape strictly matching the parent bounding box   
        this.maskShape \= scene.make.graphics({ x: x, y: y, add: false });  
        this.maskShape.fillStyle(0x000000, 1.0);  
        this.maskShape.fillRect(0, 0, width \- 20, height);  

        const geoMask \= new Phaser.Display.Masks.GeometryMask(scene, this.maskShape);  
        this.contentContainer.setMask(geoMask);

        // Render the physical scrollbar track matching the palette design   
        this.scrollbarTrack \= scene.add.graphics();  
        this.scrollbarTrack.fillStyle(0x2a1f35, 1.0);  
        this.scrollbarTrack.fillRect(width \- 12, 0, 8, height);  
        this.add(this.scrollbarTrack);

        // Render the interactive scrollbar handle  
        this.scrollbarHandle \= scene.add.graphics();  
        this.drawHandle(0x00ffcc);  
        this.scrollbarHandle.setX(width \- 12);  
        this.scrollbarHandle.setY(0);  
        this.add(this.scrollbarHandle);

        // Establish dragging area for input mapping \[4, 13\]  
        this.scrollbarHandle.setInteractive(  
            new Phaser.Geom.Rectangle(0, 0, 8, 40),  
            Phaser.Geom.Rectangle.Contains  
        );  
        scene.input.setDraggable(this.scrollbarHandle);

        // Initialize vertical dragging constraints \[13, 14, 15\]  
        scene.input.on('drag', (pointer: Phaser.Input.Pointer, gameObject: any, dragX: number, dragY: number) \=\> {  
            if (gameObject \=== this.scrollbarHandle) {  
                const minY \= 0;  
                const maxY \= this.consoleHeight \- 40;  
                const clampedY \= Phaser.Math.Clamp(dragY \- this.y, minY, maxY);  

                gameObject.setY(clampedY);  
                this.scrollPercentage \= clampedY / maxY;  
                this.updateScrollPosition();  
            }  
        });

        // Map mouse wheel delta scroll updates \[12\]  
        scene.input.on('wheel', (pointer: Phaser.Input.Pointer, currentlyOver: any, deltaX: number, deltaY: number) \=\> {  
            const worldBounds \= this.getBounds();  
            if (worldBounds.contains(pointer.x, pointer.y)) {  
                const step \= 0.05;  
                this.scrollPercentage \= Phaser.Math.Clamp(  
                    this.scrollPercentage \+ (deltaY \> 0? step : \-step),  
                    0,  
                    1  
                );  

                const handleMaxY \= this.consoleHeight \- 40;  
                this.scrollbarHandle.setY(this.scrollPercentage \* handleMaxY);  
                this.updateScrollPosition();  
            }  
        });

        scene.add.existing(this);  
    }

    private drawHandle(color: number) {  
        this.scrollbarHandle.clear();  
        this.scrollbarHandle.fillStyle(color, 1.0);  
        this.scrollbarHandle.fillRect(0, 0, 8, 40);  
    }

    public appendLog(line: string) {  
        this.textLines.push(line);  
        if (this.textLines.length \> this.maxCapacity) {  
            this.textLines.shift();  
        }

        // Wipe obsolete objects to maintain clean display lists   
        this.textObjects.forEach(obj \=\> obj.destroy());  
        this.textObjects \=;

        let verticalOffset \= this.padding;  
        for (let i \= 0; i \< this.textLines.length; i++) {  
            const textObj \= this.scene.add.text(this.padding, verticalOffset, this.textLines\[i\], {  
                fontFamily: 'Courier',  
                fontSize: '24px', // Double-scale texture size   
                color: '\#00ffcc',  
                wordWrap: { width: (this.consoleWidth \- 32) \* 2, useAdvancedWrap: true },  
                resolution: window.devicePixelRatio || 2 // Force pixel mapping   
            });  

            textObj.setScale(0.5); // Downscale to achieve crisp edges   
            this.contentContainer.add(textObj);  
            this.textObjects.push(textObj);

            // Translate logical height down to container coordinate bounds   
            verticalOffset \+= (textObj.height \* 0.5) \+ 4;  
        }

        this.snapToBottom();  
    }

    private updateScrollPosition() {  
        const totalHeight \= this.textObjects.reduce((sum, obj) \=\> sum \+ (obj.height \* 0.5) \+ 4, 0);  
        const overflow \= totalHeight \- this.consoleHeight;

        if (overflow \> 0) {  
            this.contentContainer.setY(-this.scrollPercentage \* overflow);  
        } else {  
            this.contentContainer.setY(0);  
        }  
    }

    private snapToBottom() {  
        const totalHeight \= this.textObjects.reduce((sum, obj) \=\> sum \+ (obj.height \* 0.5) \+ 4, 0);  
        const overflow \= totalHeight \- this.consoleHeight;

        if (overflow \> 0) {  
            this.scrollPercentage \= 1.0;  
            const handleMaxY \= this.consoleHeight \- 40;  
            this.scrollbarHandle.setY(handleMaxY);  
            this.contentContainer.setY(-overflow);  
        } else {  
            this.scrollPercentage \= 0;  
            this.scrollbarHandle.setY(0);  
            this.contentContainer.setY(0);  
        }  
    }

    // Coordinates the geometric mask position if the parent console undergoes translation \[1\]  
    public setPosition(x: number, y: number): this {  
        super.setPosition(x, y);  
        if (this.maskShape) {  
            this.maskShape.setPosition(x, y);  
        }  
        return this;  
    }  
}

### **In-Scene Modal Window and Proximity Collision Handlers**

Inspection mechanics mapping room environments to local server variables depend on spatial proximity checks.3 Proximity validation uses two distinct trigger approaches: explicit circular coordinate radius checks and physics engine AABB overlap queries.2

TypeScript  
export class ModalWindow extends Phaser.GameObjects.Container {  
    private frameGraphics: Phaser.GameObjects.Graphics;  
    private titleText: Phaser.GameObjects.Text;  
    private dataText: Phaser.GameObjects.Text;  
    private closeButton: Phaser.GameObjects.Graphics;

    constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene, x: number, y: number, title: string, dataContent: string) {  
        super(scene, x, y);

        // Core window frame layout using double-bevel borders  
        this.frameGraphics \= scene.add.graphics();  
        this.frameGraphics.fillStyle(0x2a1f35, 0.95);  
        this.frameGraphics.lineStyle(2, 0xff00cc, 1);  
        this.frameGraphics.fillRect(-160, \-110, 320, 220);  
        this.frameGraphics.strokeRect(-160, \-110, 320, 220);  

        // Inner double-inset channel  
        this.frameGraphics.lineStyle(1, 0x00ffcc, 0.5);  
        this.frameGraphics.strokeRect(-154, \-104, 308, 208);  
        this.add(this.frameGraphics);

        this.titleText \= scene.add.text(-140, \-90, title, {  
            fontFamily: 'Courier',  
            fontSize: '36px',  
            color: '\#00ffcc',  
            fontStyle: 'bold',  
            resolution: 2  
        }).setScale(0.5);  
        this.add(this.titleText);

        this.dataText \= scene.add.text(-140, \-50, dataContent, {  
            fontFamily: 'Courier',  
            fontSize: '24px',  
            color: '\#ffee88',  
            wordWrap: { width: 560, useAdvancedWrap: true },  
            resolution: 2  
        }).setScale(0.5);  
        this.add(this.dataText);

        // Dismiss action UI button   
        this.closeButton \= scene.add.graphics();  
        this.closeButton.fillStyle(0xff00cc, 1.0);  
        this.closeButton.fillRect(120, \-100, 20, 20);  
        this.add(this.closeButton);

        this.closeButton.setInteractive(  
            new Phaser.Geom.Rectangle(120, \-100, 20, 20),  
            Phaser.Geom.Rectangle.Contains  
        );

        this.closeButton.on('pointerdown', () \=\> {  
            this.destroy();  
        });

        scene.add.existing(this);  
    }  
}

This matrix coordinates player inspection states with spatial collision boundaries inside the room:

| Scene Entity / Zone | Trigger Coordinates (X, Y) | Radius Check Limit | Action Result |
| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |
| Core Vault | (240, 180\) | 48 pixels | Instantiates ModalWindow containing central room configuration records.3 |
| Clawforge Forge Area | (520, 320\) | 64 pixels | Displays active agent tasks, forge temperature, and pipeline status. |
| Operational Gates | (120, 450\) | 48 pixels | Displays security validation logs and proxy path statistics. |

TypeScript  
// Collision configuration setup registered inside the Main Scene structure   
export function configureInspectionTriggers(  
    scene: Phaser.Scene,   
    player: Phaser.Types.Physics.Arcade.SpriteWithDynamicBody,   
    inspectionZones: Array\<{x: number, y: number, name: string, data: string}\>  
) {  
    inspectionZones.forEach(zone \=\> {  
        const trigger \= scene.add.zone(zone.x, zone.y, 64, 64);  
        scene.physics.add.existing(trigger, true); // Set static physics sensor

        scene.physics.add.overlap(player, trigger, () \=\> {  
            const keys \= scene.input.keyboard?.createCursorKeys();  
            if (Phaser.Input.Keyboard.JustDown(keys?.space as Phaser.Input.Keyboard.Key)) {  
                // Assert singleton instantiation to prevent window redundancy   
                const existingModal \= scene.children.list.find(child \=\> child instanceof ModalWindow);  
                if (\!existingModal) {  
                    new ModalWindow(scene, scene.scale.width / 2, scene.scale.height / 2, zone.name, zone.data);  
                }  
            }  
        });  
    });  
}

### **Floating Status Indicators**

Whenever agent processes receive payload changes, floating text status notifications spawn above their coordinate centers.3

TypeScript  
export class StatusNotificationManager {  
    private scene: Phaser.Scene;

    constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene) {  
        this.scene \= scene;  
    }

    public triggerIndicator(x: number, y: number, message: string, colorHex: number) {  
        const textElement \= this.scene.add.text(x, y \- 24, message, {  
            fontFamily: 'Courier',  
            fontSize: '28px',  
            color: '\#' \+ colorHex.toString(16),  
            fontStyle: 'bold',  
            resolution: 2  
        }).setScale(0.5);  
        textElement.setOrigin(0.5, 0.5);

        // Inject dynamic WebGL Glow post-processing filter \[17, 18, 19\]  
        if (this.scene.cameras.main.renderer.type \=== Phaser.WEBGL) {  
            textElement.postFX.addGlow(colorHex, 4, 0, false, 0.1, 16);  
        }

        // Apply upward velocity and linear alpha decay   
        this.scene.tweens.add({  
            targets: textElement,  
            y: y \- 72,  
            alpha: 0.0,  
            duration: 900,  
            ease: 'Cubic.easeOut',  
            onComplete: () \=\> {  
                textElement.destroy();  
            }  
        });  
    }  
}

## **Asynchronous WebSocket Synchronization and Delta Parsing**

Asynchronous synchronization requires continuous network communication decoupled from visual frame updates to prevent stuttering in the underlying rendering cycles.3 The WebSocket client handles connection tracking, state updates, and mapping network data directly to on-screen components.3

┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  
│               Python Multi-Agent Core                  │  
│               \[Gateway Port: 18789\]                    │  
└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘  
                           │ (Asynchronous WSS Payload)  
                           ▼  
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  
│                RavenstackWSClient                      │  
│                \[Frontend Port: 8080\]                   │  
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤  
│  Heartbeat: Ping/Pong (10s decay, 30s probe)           │  
│  State Machine: Active Sync / Error Backoff Jitter     │  
└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘  
                           │ (Direct State Delta Events)  
                           ▼  
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  
│               Phaser 3 Display List                    │  
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤  
│  1\. Sprite Frame Switcher                              │  
│  2\. WebGL Glow Filter Intensity Tweens                 │  
│  3\. Tween-driven Kinematic Coordinate Shifts            │  
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

The parsed JSON packets match the schema of the centralized castle\_map.json deployment file.3

### **Castle Map payload schema definition**

| JSON Node Pathway | Expected Data Type | Architectural Purpose |
| :---- | :---- | :---- |
| timestamp | Number (Int64) | Epoch verification parameter to identify and ignore delayed packet arrivals. |
| rooms | Array\<RoomObject\> | Sequential array listing active room boundaries and security levels. |
| rooms.roomId | String | Unique alphanumeric string targeting physical coordinates. |
| rooms.agents | Array\<AgentObject\> | Array listing the current states of agents inside the room.3 |
| rooms.agents.id | String | Unique persistent identification string mapping directly to game entities. |
| rooms.agents.state | String ('idle'|'typing'|'error'|'working') | Operational state that maps to animation frames and glow filters.3 |
| rooms.agents.x | Number (Float32) | Target X-coordinate on the room layout map. |
| rooms.agents.y | Number (Float32) | Target Y-coordinate on the room layout map. |

### **Robust TypeScript WebSocket Client Class**

TypeScript  
export interface WSUpdatePayload {  
    timestamp: number;  
    rooms: Array\<{  
        roomId: string;  
        agents: Array\<{  
            id: string;  
            state: 'idle' | 'typing' | 'error' | 'working';  
            x: number;  
            y: number;  
        }\>;  
    }\>;  
}

export class RavenstackWSClient {  
    private url: string \= 'ws://100.119.160.116:18789';  
    private ws\!: WebSocket;  
    private scene: Phaser.Scene;  

    private isConnected: boolean \= false;  
    private reconnectAttempts: number \= 0;  
    private maxBackoffDelay: number \= 30000;  
    private baseDelay: number \= 1000;

    private pingInterval: number \= 30000; // 30s heartbeat probe \[21\]  
    private pongTimeout: number \= 10000;  // 10s packet decay \[22\]  
    private heartbeatTimer?: any;  
    private disconnectTimer?: any;

    private lossOverlay?: Phaser.GameObjects.Container;  
    public onDeltaParsed?: (payload: WSUpdatePayload) \=\> void;

    constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene) {  
        this.scene \= scene;  
        this.connect();  
    }

    private connect() {  
        this.ws \= new WebSocket(this.url);  
        this.ws.onopen \= () \=\> this.onOpen();  
        this.ws.onmessage \= (event) \=\> this.onMessage(event);  
        this.ws.onclose \= () \=\> this.onClose();  
        this.ws.onerror \= () \=\> this.ws.close();  
    }

    private onOpen() {  
        this.isConnected \= true;  
        this.reconnectAttempts \= 0;  
        this.clearLossOverlay();  
        this.startHeartbeat();  
    }

    private onMessage(event: MessageEvent) {  
        try {  
            const data \= JSON.parse(event.data);

            // Treat application-level keep-alive response structures \[21, 22\]  
            if (data.type \=== 'PONG') {  
                clearTimeout(this.disconnectTimer);  
                return;  
            }

            if (data.timestamp && data.rooms) {  
                if (this.onDeltaParsed) {  
                    this.onDeltaParsed(data as WSUpdatePayload);  
                }  
            }  
        } catch (e) {  
            // Mitigate dirty payload parsing faults silently  
        }  
    }

    private onClose() {  
        this.isConnected \= false;  
        this.stopHeartbeat();  
        this.renderLossOverlay();  
        this.scheduleReconnection();
